    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-37264",
      "knowledge_point_id": "b0e5efaa-e624-5045-abdb-cdf8d32ad6cb",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying Subsets of a Given Set",
      "problem": "Which of the following sets is a subset of $A={4n+1∣n\\in {0,1,2,3}}?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we must find the elements of the set $A.$ Substituting the values $n\\in {0,1,2,3}$ into the formula $4n+1,$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=0 & \\,⇒\\,4(0)+1=1 \\\\ n=1 & \\,⇒\\,4(1)+1=5 \\\\ n=2 & \\,⇒\\,4(2)+1=9 \\\\ n=3 & \\,⇒\\,4(3)+1=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA={1,5,9,13}.\n$$\n\nNow, a subset of $A$ is a set whose elements are also elements of the set $A.$\n\nIn our case, $B={1,5,13}$ is a subset of $A.$\n\nIn the rest of the options, the set $B$ has elements that are not in $A,$ meaning that it is not a subset of $A.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "B={1,5,13}"
            },
