      "problem": "Find all of the subsets of $S={r,t}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find every subset of $S,$ we list out every combination of elements within $S.$\n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/assets/022399e6a7a5e1f79b58e856aa8e9e5e9f3561e8e4bcb5b80a95237d30d06002.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,{r},{t},{r,t}.\n$$",
