      "knowledge_point_id": "9b7f1d12-3335-5dd7-bf36-e07077d0c45d",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying Subsets of Special Sets",
      "problem": "Which of the following are subsets of ${R}^{-}$ (the set of negative real numbers)?\n\n- ${Z}_{0}^{-}$ (the set of non-positive integers)\n- $N$\n- ${Q}^{-}$  (the set of negative rational numbers)",
      "worked_solution": "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Z}_{0}^{-}$ is *not* a subset of ${R}^{-}.$ For example, $0\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}$ but $0\\notin {R}^{-}.$\n\n- $N$ is not  a subset of ${R}^{-}.$ For example, $1\\in N$ but $1\\notin {R}^{-}.$\n\n- ${Q}^{-}$ is a subset of ${R}^{-}.$ Indeed, every negative rational number is also a negative real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
