      "problem": "Which of the following are subsets of $R?$\n\n- ${Q}^{+}$ (the set of positive rationals)\n- ${Z}^{-}$ (the set of negative integers)\n- $N$",
      "worked_solution": "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Q}^{+}$ is  a subset of $R.$ Every positive rational number is a real number.\n\n- ${Z}^{-}$ is a subset of $R.$ Every negative integer number is a real number.\n\n- $N$ a subset of $R.$ Every natural number is a real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\".",
